        <p class="profile-detail-region">City · Central &amp; East Asia</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Karakorum</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">1220 CE – c. 1400 CE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a> rallied his troops at a place called Karakorum in 1218 and 1219, and the foundation of the city is usually said to have occurred in 1220. His successor Ögedei built city walls and a fixed palace from 1235.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">In the upper Orkhon Valley, in the north-western corner of the Övörkhangai Province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongolia">Mongolia</a>, near the present town of Kharkhorin.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">Capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a> from 1235 to 1260; the Palace of Myriad Peace; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">Silver</a> Tree of Guillaume Boucher; the account of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-of-rubruck">William of Rubruck</a>, who reached it in 1254; the great stupa temple; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erdene-zuu">Erdene Zuu Monastery</a> built from its stones</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">The ruins lie beside the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erdene-zuu">Erdene Zuu Monastery</a> in the upper part of the Orkhon Valley <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/world-heritage-site">World Heritage Site</a>, near the town of Kharkhorin.</span></div>
        </div>
